ceSha1":"0279b6c7f12cfd8159f385a281e494fab3a9231c","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"Historic front exterior"}],"aliases":[],"authors":["Open Landmarks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["All mass centres and lower plans come from the saved OSM building:part polygons. The tapered aisle plan, long nave, rear apse, four octagonal turrets, front piers and lantern columns remain registered to those parts.","Mapped heights are retained: aisle 25 m; nave eave/ridge 35/40 m; corner turret eave/dome 40/45 m; main drum/dome 45/70 m; lantern platforms 71/72/78.5 m and terminal lantern roof 83 m. The main dome is still 70 m and the overall height remains 83 m.","Individually inspected Commons references 00 and 04 establish the three deep front arches, full-width sculpture frieze, large rose with concentric tracery, Romanesque upper nave bays, octagonal turret arcades, paneled hemispheroidal dome with ribs, and slender copper lantern. Reference 04 is a historical exterior and is used only to clarify the front elevation.","Porch spring 10.6 m, porch upper slab 15.2 m, rose centre 27 m/radius 5.1 m, drum window proportions, dome rib count 16 and turret ornament are proportional inferences from photographs, not survey dimensions. Sculpture is represented by abstract masses. Dome profile is a source-informed ellipse scaled to the existing mapped 25 m roof height; no source heights are silently revised.","Only opaque shared-library stone, trim, slate roof, window and copper finishes are used. All vertical windows have constructed stone supporting faces. The lantern retains real openings between mapped columns; sloped dome panels remain roof/trim geometry rather than unsupported window glass.","Low LOD is separately authored: mapped silhouette, three-arch porch, rose, eight thickened main dome ribs, principal nave/drum windows and lantern are retained; fine coursing, sculptures, secondary window surrounds and most roof seams are removed."],"source":{"url":"/objects/0ea79b01edf4435da9bd51968d959b623fab46e0e63c98167b0a258223f8b38d/source.blend.gz","bytes":629415,"sha256":"0ea79b01edf4435da9bd51968d959b623fab46e0e63c98167b0a258223f8b38d"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/367fe8b2cf3129c2227deb9f7be2172b46a85ba9c585facb09e0904c8b0089ed/spatial-source.json","bytes":44896,"sha256":"367fe8b2cf3129c2227deb9f7be2172b46a85ba9c585facb09e0904c8b0089ed"},"preview":{"url":"/objects/042bb0ca51215821c2d247127c1b007e0e377e3cef29c4abd25737057336dcda/preview.webp","bytes":12844,"sha256":"042bb0ca51215821c2d247127c1b007e0e377e3cef29c4abd25737057336dcda"},"revision":"a89a026be0a665a6544a69934cbc1c732f0e5fa605d1acacba84fe7025ff0674","publicationRevision":"176b598d697c07cfd9fc3a36b002439fcf8f80b17c4485169a463e139221faa3","bounds":[2.3184558,48.8757874,2.3192953,48.8766011],"approved":false,"materialLibrary":{"schemaVersion":1,"sha256":"f1d437b52bbae89b4d9ee6420ea21fefbf88b8682a9254cd0b052421b0c99647","url":"/materials/f1d437b52bbae89b4d9ee6420ea21fefbf88b8682a9254cd0b052421b0c99647.json"},"metadata":"/assets/saint-augustin/176b598d697c07cfd9fc3a36b002439fcf8f80b17c4485169a463e139221faa3/asset.json","validation":"/assets/saint-augustin/176b598d697c07cfd9fc3a36b002439fcf8f80b17c4485169a463e139221faa3/validation.json"}